  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nMarked price = 2,500\n\nSuccessive discounts = 25%, 20%, K%\n\nSelling price = 1,380\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nSelling Price = MP × (1 − d₁) × (1 − d₂) × (1 − d₃)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ Selling price = 2500 × (1 − 25/100) × (1 − 20/100) × (1 − K/100)\n\n⇒ 1380 = 2500 × 0.75 × 0.80 × (1 − K/100)\n\n⇒ 1380 = 2500 × 0.60 × (1 − K/100)\n\n⇒ 1380 = 1500 × (1 − K/100)\n\n⇒ 1 − K/100 = 1380 ÷ 1500\n\n⇒ 1 − K/100 = 0.92\n\n⇒ K/100 = 1 − 0.92\n\n⇒ K/100 = 0.08\n\n⇒ K = 8\n\n**∴ The correct value of K is 8%.**\n\n54:T8a",
